00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:50.260
Carly Huitema (University of Guelph): We have different ways to develop identifiers. The 1st one I'm going to mention is assigned, or name identifiers. It's very common. We're certainly all familiar with it, and that is where some kind of governance body is going to create an identifier for some specific object, and they also might add additional metadata to help describe the object. And what that governance body is going to do is they have to create what I've called down below the lookup table.

101
00:17:50.260 --> 00:17:56.310
Carly Huitema (University of Guelph): They have the identifier, and then its location where you can go and find it, and maybe some additional metadata.

