104
00:18:46.780 --> 00:19:05.790
Carly Huitema (University of Guelph): In contrast to assigned identifiers. We really like derived identifiers. They are really important for reproducibility and authenticity, because with a derived identifier, what you're doing is that it works for digital objects. And what you do is you are calculating the hash.

